WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.935 --> 00:00:16.516
Mowgli continued growing and learning the law of the jungle.

2
00:00:18.816 --> 00:00:21.337
One year a terrible drought arrived.

3
00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:25.578
It began when the winter came, bringing little rain.

4
00:00:28.799 --> 00:00:32.040
The yams dried up and few trees flowered.

5
00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:40.672
Next a burning heat crept into the jungle, turning it yellow, brown, and then black.

6
00:00:42.453 --> 00:00:43.993
Water holes turned to mud.

7
00:00:47.956 --> 00:00:52.258
Bamboo stalks grew dry, clanking loudly in the hot wind.

8
00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.582
It was the first time that Mowgli had felt deep hunger.

9
00:01:01.923 --> 00:01:05.225
While this hunger was awful, his thirst was worse.

10
00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:10.949
The heat went on and on, drying up all the moisture.

11
00:01:14.531 --> 00:01:17.473
Soon only one river still had water.

12
00:01:20.154 --> 00:01:23.757
Hathi, the wise old elephant, lifted his trunk.

13
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.259
"There is a water truce!"

14
00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:28.460
he declared.

15
00:01:30.268 --> 00:01:33.831
Mowgli learned that this meant no one could hunt at the river.

16
00:01:34.711 --> 00:01:37.913
Instead everyone could safely drink there.

17
00:01:39.754 --> 00:01:44.037
The animals whistled and shrieked, spreading the news of the water truce.

18
00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.743
is a terrible time," Bagheera said one evening at the river.

19
00:01:54.524 --> 00:01:55.365
Mowgli nodded.

20
00:01:56.085 --> 00:01:58.547
The air still felt as hot as fire.

21
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.101
Baloo sighed.

22
00:02:01.902 --> 00:02:04.404
"The rains have forgotten us this year."

23
00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:11.050
Upstream, Hathi stood with his sons in the moonlight.

24
00:02:12.391 --> 00:02:16.955
Nearby some deer were drinking, along with pigs and wild buffalo.

25
00:02:16.975 --> 00:02:21.619
"The humans are hungry too," a pig said.

26
00:02:21.639 --> 00:02:24.562
"They're dying in their fields."

27
00:02:24.582 --> 00:02:30.225
"Hathi, have you ever seen anything like this drought?"

28
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:31.485
Baloo asked.

29
00:02:32.505 --> 00:02:34.726
"No. But it will pass."

30
00:02:35.746 --> 00:02:38.867
Hathi squirted water along his back and sides.

31
00:02:41.168 --> 00:02:42.548
Baloo looked at Mowgli.

32
00:02:42.568 --> 00:02:48.750
"Well, we have someone here who cannot survive much longer without more food.

33
00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.251
The boy is all skin and bones."

34
00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:56.692
"Hey!" Mowgli sat up in the water, insulted.

35
00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.061
"That's because I don't have any fur to cover my bones."

36
00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:07.184
Everyone laughed, but Mowgli was scowling at Baloo.

37
00:03:07.204 --> 00:03:10.846
"You wouldn't look good without fur either!"

38
00:03:12.426 --> 00:03:16.828
Bagheera put out a paw and gently knocked Mowgli back into the water.

39
00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:21.990
Mowgli rose, spluttering and laughing.

40
00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:27.473
"It's rude to make fun of your teacher, Mowgli," Bagheera said.

41
00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.255
Grinning, he dunked Mowgli again.

42
00:03:32.556 --> 00:03:38.360
This time when Mowgli rose from the water, he saw that Bagheera's expression had changed.

43
00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.042
"Uh-oh," he thought.

44
00:03:41.703 --> 00:03:44.244
He saw the tiger slinking toward them.

45
00:03:47.406 --> 00:03:49.148
"Why, look at this."

46
00:03:50.048 --> 00:03:52.410
Shere Khan's voice was a low rumble.

47
00:03:53.711 --> 00:03:55.072
He bent to take a drink.

48
00:03:55.972 --> 00:03:57.553
"It's the man cub."

49
00:03:59.335 --> 00:04:03.878
Mowgli slipped behind Bagheera as Shere Khan dipped his chin in the river.

50
00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:08.681
Soon dark oily streaks were floating in the water.

51
00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:13.405
Bagheera looked suspiciously at the oily streaks.

52
00:04:14.566 --> 00:04:16.467
"What have you been up to, Shere Khan?"

53
00:04:17.628 --> 00:04:19.429
Shere Khan smiled slyly.

54
00:04:19.449 --> 00:04:23.072
"I found a human," he said.

55
00:04:23.772 --> 00:04:28.535
"So I came to the river for a drink—and to clean myself."

56
00:04:30.777 --> 00:04:32.338
A few animals gasped.

57
00:04:32.358 --> 00:04:37.582
"You killed a person during the drought?"

58
00:04:38.022 --> 00:04:39.003
Bagheera snapped.

59
00:04:39.023 --> 00:04:41.724
"Couldn't you find something else to eat?"

60
00:04:42.805 --> 00:04:44.546
The tiger just shrugged.

61
00:04:46.147 --> 00:04:48.009
Hathi had been listening quietly.

62
00:04:52.192 --> 00:04:56.517
Now he stepped closer to Shere Khan and swung his trunk.

63
00:04:56.537 --> 00:05:02.219
"As you know, Shere Khan, there is a drought," the elephant said.

64
00:05:02.239 --> 00:05:06.740
"The river is for drinking, not washing off blood.

65
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.561
Besides, we are all suffering—jungle animals and humans.

66
00:05:13.482 --> 00:05:16.022
It is wrong to boast of killing right now."

67
00:05:17.343 --> 00:05:18.783
Shere Khan looked down.

68
00:05:18.803 --> 00:05:22.064
"Have you had enough to drink?"

69
00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.169
Hathi asked.

70
00:05:23.969 --> 00:05:26.331
"Yes." "Go then!"

71
00:05:26.832 --> 00:05:27.853
Hathi commanded.

72
00:05:30.275 --> 00:05:32.917
His three sons moved to stand behind him.

73
00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.183
Shere Khan slunk away, not even daring to growl.

74
00:05:41.104 --> 00:05:46.108
For he knew what everyone knew—Hathi was the master of the jungle.

75
00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.532
Bagheera sighed and turned back to Mowgli.

76
00:05:51.556 --> 00:05:53.239
"Never forget this, Little Brother.

77
00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.124
Shere Khan is your enemy."
